-- title:
--   Residual Hecke characters are trivial on the diamond operators
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $\bar\rho.V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from the group of $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(\bar\rho.V)$ which is trivial on all automorphisms fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible: after base change to an algebraic closure of $k$ the only submodules stable under all $\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ are $\bot$ and $\top$. Fix $M\neq 0$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, a finite set $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ with $p\in S$, and $a:\mathbb N\to k$ such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ equals $X^2-a_\ell X+\ell$. Let $F$ be a field, $\iota:k\to F$ a ring homomorphism, and let $\psi$ be a ring homomorphism to $F$ from the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(\mathrm{CohCarrier.H1}\ M\ H\ \mathcal O)$ generated by the operators [`CohCarrier.heckeTL M H 𝒪 ℓ`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M$ (pre-composition with conjugation by the upper-triangular matrix attached to $\ell$, followed by the transfer from the subgroup $\mathrm{GammaHUpper}\ M\ H\ \ell$) together with all diamond operators [`CohCarrier.diamondL M H 𝒪 d`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55), $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ (pre-composition with conjugation by a chosen lift of $d$ to $\Gamma_0(M)$). Assume $\psi$ restricts on $\mathcal O$ to $\iota$ composed with reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and $\psi(\mathrm{heckeTL}\ M\ H\ \mathcal O\ \ell)=\iota(a_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M$. Then $\psi(\mathrm{diamondL}\ M\ H\ \mathcal O\ d)=1$ for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$.
--
--   This is the residual form of Carayol's comparison between the nebentypus of a weight-two eigenform and the determinant of its associated Galois representation: a Hecke character of the cohomology carrier whose $T_\ell$-values match the Frobenius traces of an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$ with cyclotomic determinant is trivial on the diamond operators. It is used in the Taylor–Wiles level bookkeeping, by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.toML_diamondL_eq_toML`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.toML_diamondL_eq_toML).
